       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Amlodipine 50 mg daily is five times the maximum dose, and I can't find a clinical situation where it would be appropriate. Your message also didn't give a reason for the dose. The risk is serious harm to the patient: profound hypotension and shock that may last a long time, and noncardiogenic pulmonary edema.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter 10 mg by mouth once daily**, the maximum labeled dose. I can do that now. If you need more blood pressure control, adding a second agent from a different class is the usual approach.\n- **Enter 5 mg by mouth once daily**, if you meant the standard starting dose.\n- **Talk to pharmacy or your attending** if you think there's an unusual reason for a higher dose. If the order is then confirmed through those channels, it can be entered directly or with their involvement.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
